# Browser service configuration. No cloud credentials are used.
# The defaults use the same origin as the application, including in local installs.
# Absolute overrides add their service origins to the production connection policy.
# Copy to .env.local for development or .env.production for a production build.
# Mount at / locally or at /almanac/ behind a portfolio reverse proxy.
VITE_BASE_PATH=/
# Service and worklet defaults inherit the mount path.
# VITE_PROXY_BASE=/v1
# VITE_STT_BASE=/api/asr-http
# TTS defaults to ws(s)://<application-host>/<mount>/api/tts_streaming.
# VITE_TTS_BASE=wss://<speech-host>/api/tts_streaming

# Optional voice tuning (self-hosters). All fall back to sane defaults.
#   VITE_TTS_VOICE      voice id your TTS server knows (default: alba)
#   VITE_TTS_AUTH       token sent as the auth_id query param, if your endpoint checks one
#   VITE_TTS_CFG_ALPHA  classifier-free-guidance strength (default 1.5)
#   VITE_STT_AUTH       bearer token if your Whisper endpoint is auth-gated (default none)
# VITE_TTS_VOICE=
# VITE_TTS_AUTH=
# VITE_TTS_CFG_ALPHA=
# VITE_STT_AUTH=

# Voice-concurrency broker. Leave off (0) for a single TTS endpoint — the browser
# connects straight to VITE_STT_BASE/VITE_TTS_BASE. Set to 1 only when running
# several TTS endpoints behind the proxy's /voice/* broker (leased endpoints +
# overflow queue), which also requires the proxy's voice config.
VITE_VOICE_BROKER=0
